  #KRT-102 : Configuring the crontab in krait through .cron file. Crontab data should be kept in a file *.cron (krait_conf.cron) and provide the file name as argument to the command "crontab". The data in the *.cron file should be exactly as the crontab format so that everything present in that file will be replaced in the crontab of a machine. 
Note : provide the obsolute path of *.cron if it is present in any other location than the location from where the command is executed.

And this file can be modified and can be executed in the future also for any crontab data updates in krait.
